translated_text:
Second Part
Prevention of Acts of Violence Article 16 (1) The Regional Government conducts prevention of acts of violence against women by means of:
a. socializing laws and regulations;
b. conducting empowerment and awareness raising to families, parents and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling; c. conducting efforts to increase the quantity and quality of education both formal and non-formal and informal;
d. conducting efforts to build community participation and concern to implement prevention and protection of women and children from violence in an integrated community-based manner;
e. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities, religious institutions/organizations and various non-governmental organizations in efforts to prevent violence against women and children;
f. establishing a violence prevention system, mapping of locations or areas prone to violence;
g. increasing community awareness that respects women and protects children;
h. establishing UPTD PPA in every Sub-district, and Service Posts for the Protection of Women and Children at the Village and Sub-district levels; and
i. establishing a task force for the protection of women and children.
(2) In addition to the Regional Government, prevention as referred to in paragraph (1) must be implemented by:
a. family and/or closest relatives;
b. the community;
c. vertical agencies;
d. law enforcement apparatus;
e. educational institutions;
f. health institutions;
g. religious institutions/organizations;
h. social community institutions;
i. the business sector; and
j. other institutions.
(3) Prevention of acts of violence against women as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be conducted in an integrated manner and coordinated by the Regional Apparatus that has the main duties and functions in the field of women's empowerment and child protection.

