Third Part
Integrated Services for Victims of Violence Article 8 (1) The Regional Government implements integrated services for Victims of Violence, through activities:
a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. Counseling;
d. psychological services;
e. spiritual guidance;
f. social rehabilitation services;
g. legal aid and assistance services;
h. safe house services; and/or
i. repatriation and social reintegration.
(2) In the event that the Regional Government does not yet have counseling personnel as referred to in paragraph (1) letter c, it may request assistance from social workers, volunteer assistants, and/or spiritual counselors.
(3) Services as referred to in paragraph (1) must be supported by facilities in the form of:
a. special service rooms within the police force;
b. expert and professional personnel;
c. service centers and Safe Houses; and/or
d. other facilities and infrastructure necessary for the recovery of victims including perpetrators.
(4) The provision of services to Victims of Violence is carried out in an integrated manner by the Regional Government together with other social institutions. (5) Other social institutions as referred to in paragraph (4) may receive and send case referrals from other service units in a networked manner. (6) Integrated Services for victims of violence as referred to in paragraphs (1) through (5) are implemented in accordance with standard operating procedures.
(7) Provisions regarding standard operating procedures as referred to in paragraph (6) are regulated in a Regent Regulation.
Article 9 (1) Complaint services as referred to in Article 8 paragraph (1) letter a are implemented to receive reports of acts of violence.
(2) Reports as referred to in paragraph (1) may originate from: a. victims;
b. referrals; or
c. outreach.

