Article 10
(1) Health services as referred to in Article 8 paragraph - (1) letter b, are implemented using health facilities owned by the Regional Government or other referral hospitals by providing treatment services and health recovery for victims.
(2) Health services as referred to in paragraph (1) are carried out by health workers for victims in accordance with professional standards, operational procedure standards and the medical needs of victims.
(3) Health services as referred to in paragraph (1), through efforts: a. anamnesis of victims;
b. examination of victims;
c. providing first aid;
d. health recovery both physical and psychological, carrying out efforts to prevent disease and other health disorders;
e. counseling;
f. referring to more adequate health service facilities if necessary can refer to other parties with a multidisciplinary approach, including health services, medicolegal, psychosocial assistance and legal aid; and/or
g. providing information to the police.
(4) In addition to the efforts as referred to in paragraph (3) for certain cases, health workers may provide reproductive health services in accordance with medical needs.
(5) In providing services as referred to in paragraph (3) and paragraph (4), health workers must make medical records in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations, (6) For every medical action to be carried out by health workers there must be consent for medical action from the victim or their family in accordance with the provisions of laws and regulations.
(7) For investigation purposes, authorized health workers must make a visum et repertum and/or visum et repertum psichiatricum. or make a medical certificate.
(8) Health workers have the right to obtain legal protection.
Article11 Legal aid and protection services as referred to in Article 8 paragraph (1) letter g include:
a. providing protection in Safe Houses;
b. providing legal information to Victims;
c. providing Assistance for Victims as witnesses from the investigation process to the verdict;
d. providing special legal protection for child victims of violence can be carried out by appointing guardianship in accordance with laws and regulations.
Article12 (1) Repatriation and social reintegration as referred to in Article 8 paragraph (1) letter g are implemented with the following principles:
a. voluntary;
b. safe and dignified; and
c. respect for rights.
(2) In the event that the Regional Government is not yet able to implement repatriation and social reintegration as referred to in paragraph (1) it may request assistance from related parties.
(3) Social services to administer social welfare for Children in conflict with the law are carried out by the Regional Government together with LPKS and other social institutions.
(4) LPKS and other social institutions as referred to in paragraph (3) are rehabilitation and temporary shelter places for children in conflict with the law before repatriation and social reintegration are implemented.

